Falsifies `paging::aarch64::verification::no_encoded_leaf_is_both_writable_and_executable`.

The defect: `Aarch64::attrs` stops setting `PXN` on a writable page, on the reasoning that a data
page is not code and the kernel will never branch into it. That is the reasoning W^X exists to
refuse. The portable `Flags` constructors already keep write and execute apart, so a writable page
reaching the encoder is a page whose descriptor must carry `PXN`, or a kernel buffer overflow in
`kernel_data` gains an instruction pointer at EL1.

Expected to fail: the harness's only assertion, on `Flags::kernel_data()` (AP[2] clear, PXN clear).

